**Read:** [GSAS-II — diffraction analysis and refinement tutorials](../sources/GSAS-II-Refinement-Tutorials.lingua#r_14B5VSDN6YR5MQJVNTKYJXF3XB), the complete named tutorials and their method documentation; [A laboratory manual for X-ray powder diffraction — Poppe and colleagues](../sources/USGS-X-ray-Powder-Diffraction-Manual.lingua#r_3S2AET1HS289HRQBDJ87A30DX6), the full relevant phase-identification context; [Measurement and metrology](../../../../hephaestus/inquiry/metrology/Metrology.lingua#r_3G54ENPA974K19AB5XF0P641N5), calibration, correlation, and model uncertainty as needed.

Whole-pattern refinement fits a specified model to observations, including structure/phase contributions, instrument behavior, profile shape, background, and corrections. A low residual measures agreement under that model and weighting; it does not independently prove a unique mineral assemblage or a physically meaningful parameter set.

Correlated parameters can compensate for one another. Preferred orientation, microabsorption, unmodelled phases, an inappropriate background, or an instrument error may bias phase proportions or structural quantities. Formal estimated uncertainties under the fit model do not automatically include these model/systematic effects.

Quantitative phase fractions need an identified basis and treatment of amorphous/unobserved material. Fractions normalized among detected crystalline phases do not necessarily represent the whole specimen. A successful synthetic example does not establish the same detection and accuracy for a difficult natural mixture.

**Work:** complete the fluoroapatite, simulation, background/limits, and publication/CIF tutorials. Explain the refinement sequence, compare residual structure and parameter correlations, test a plausible alternate model, and check a known or independently measured material proportion where available. Preserve raw data, model, settings, versions, and conditions in the study workspace.

Read the full method documentation and primary paper relevant to the specific refinement. Report fit, identifiability, calibration, and geological interpretation as separate conclusions. External software and its datasets remain study references rather than a new required Lince component.

**Continue:** [Read a CIF as a traceable model and compare it with its original evidence](Read-and-test-a-crystal-structure-record.lingua#r_1SVFJVQWKZM86VHF3Z5Y2XWVX1).

**Return:** [Mineralogy and petrology — minerals, crystals, rock processes, and investigation](../Mineralogy-and-petrology.lingua#r_44F7X6GPMW6ZSCCN6D71QSVKBN).
